 \section{System Architecture and Methodology}
 \label{sec:methodology}
 
-TERRA (historically named Temporal-Evolution and Reasoning-Trace RAG) is designed as a two-phase, closed-loop GraphRAG architecture for temporal legal reasoning on historical common-law jurisprudence. The core engineering philosophy strictly separates offline corpus ingestion and knowledge structure construction from online query routing and inference. Citation extraction, procedural-scaffold construction and indexing are performed offline; retrieval, HARD-route graph traversal, entailment grading and generation are online operations. The evaluated Category~A and Category~B queries have different latency profiles (median \TerraFastPathMedianSeconds~s on factual lookups vs. \TerraHardPathMedianSeconds~s on multi-hop citation chains; Figure~\ref{fig:system_architecture}).
